{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtoimplementservice"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" to match your privacy, residency, and batching needs — without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" in your app."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest"],"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the configuration boundary: every Mixpanel knob worth setting at launch is a parameter on the initializer, and runtime GDPR \/ diagnostic toggles are methods on the service. The Mixpanel SDK stays a private implementation detail of this package."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Default initialization","anchor":"Default-initialization"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most apps:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-token\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults match the Mixpanel SDK’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelOptions"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flushInterval: 60"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault: false"},{"type":"text","text":", gzip on, IDFV-based distinct ID, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackAutomaticEvents: false"},{"type":"text","text":". The initializer is the same on every platform."}]},{"name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Mixpanel SDK keys instances by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instanceName"},{"type":"text","text":" (falling back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":"). Constructing a second service with the same name returns the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"existing"}]},{"type":"text","text":" SDK instance and silently ignores the new options. Construct the service once, where the store is configured — not per view, per preview, or per test."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"EU \/ India data residency","anchor":"EU--India-data-residency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"serverURL:"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    serverURL: \"https:\/\/api-eu.mixpanel.com\"  \/\/ or \"https:\/\/api-in.mixpanel.com\"",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Region is fixed at construction; the service has no per-event region knob."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Opt-out by default","anchor":"Opt-out-by-default"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your jurisdiction requires explicit opt-in, construct the service in opted-out mode and flip it at runtime when the user consents:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    optOutTrackingByDefault: true",")","","\/\/ later, when the user opts in:","await service.optInTracking(distinctID: currentUserID)","","\/\/ to opt out again:","await service.optOutTracking()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optInTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/hasOptedOutTracking()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" cover the GDPR round-trip without forcing the app to touch Mixpanel directly. Pair these with the plugin’s own opt-out flag if you maintain one — both must be opted in for events to be sent."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Custom device IDs","anchor":"Custom-device-IDs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default Mixpanel derives the anonymous device ID from the IDFV (or a random UUID with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"useUniqueDistinctId: true"},{"type":"text","text":"), which does not survive app reinstall. If your app maintains its own stable device identity — for example a Keychain-minted UUID hydrated into state at launch — hand it to the SDK with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIdProvider:"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Cache the ID at launch; the provider must not do I\/O inline.","let deviceID = keychainStore.value(.deviceID) ?? mintAndStoreDeviceID()","","let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    deviceIdProvider: { deviceID }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK calls the closure synchronously while holding internal locks — at first launch (when no persisted identity exists), on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset()"},{"type":"text","text":", and on opt-out — so it must be fast: return a cached value, never Keychain or network reads. Return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" to fall back to the SDK default. Returning the same value every call keeps the device ID stable across resets; returning a fresh value gives ephemeral identities."}]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Adding a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIdProvider"},{"type":"text","text":" to an app that already shipped with the default device ID changes the anonymous identity on that device. The SDK logs a warning when the provided value differs from the persisted one."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Flush interval","anchor":"Flush-interval"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-token\", flushInterval: 30)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" (called on app shutdown) bypasses this and forces a synchronous drain."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Diagnostic logging","anchor":"Diagnostic-logging"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["await service.setLoggingEnabled(true)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enables the Mixpanel SDK’s internal logging — useful when verifying integration in development. Disable in release builds."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Geo by IP","anchor":"Geo-by-IP"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["await service.setUseIPAddressForGeoLocation(false)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt out of server-side IP-based geo resolution when your privacy policy forbids it."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Exclude properties","anchor":"Exclude-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strip named property keys from outgoing events and People "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$set"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$set_once"},{"type":"text","text":" updates before the SDK stores or sends them — a construction-time guard against PII leaking through event properties:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    excludeProperties: [\"email\", \"full_name\"]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Excluded keys are dropped by the Mixpanel SDK itself, so the rule holds no matter which mapper or reducer produced the event. Other People operators ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$append"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$unset"},{"type":"text","text":", …) pass through unfiltered, and keys Mixpanel requires for ingestion ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":", …) are never stripped even if listed."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Multiple instances","anchor":"Multiple-instances"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your app sends to more than one Mixpanel project, give each a unique "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instanceName"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let prodService = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"prod-token\",","    instanceName: \"prod\"",")","let internalService = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"internal-token\",","    instanceName: \"internal\"",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" per service. Each plugin owns its own state slice."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Escape hatch: build your own `MixpanelInstance`","anchor":"Escape-hatch-build-your-own-MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For configuration the initializer does not surface — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProxyServerConfig"},{"type":"text","text":", custom delegates, anything that requires direct access to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/init(instance:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Mixpanel  \/\/ only required for this advanced path","","let instance = Mixpanel.initialize(","    options: MixpanelOptions(","        token: \"your-token\",","        proxyServerConfig: myProxyConfig","    )",")","let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(instance: instance)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the only path that requires importing Mixpanel into your app. If you find yourself reaching for it for something common (an SDK knob the initializer should surface), please open an issue — the goal is to keep the happy path Mixpanel-free."}]}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"How to Implement the Service","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/init(instance:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Escape hatch for apps that need to construct their own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(for example, to use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProxyServerConfig"},{"type":"text","text":"). Most apps should prefer the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token-based initializer above and never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","title":"init(instance:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"instance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Mixpanel0A8InstanceC","text":"MixpanelInstance"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/init(instance:)","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/init(instance:)"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/ServiceReference":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — the Mixpanel-backed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that the analytics plugin consumes."}],"type":"topic","title":"Service Reference","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/servicereference"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" internally so apps never need to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"topic","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToPreviewAndTest":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" from SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites without touching Mixpanel’s network."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtopreviewandtest","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","kind":"article","title":"How to Preview and Test","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/ValueTranslation":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" cases map onto Mixpanel’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelType"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Properties"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","title":"Value Translation","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/valuetranslation"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/GettingStarted":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the package, build "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" with your token, register the analytics plugin, and start dispatching events."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/gettingstarted","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/hasOptedOutTracking()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hasOptedOutTracking"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" if the user has been opted out."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/hasoptedouttracking()","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/hasOptedOutTracking()","type":"topic","title":"hasOptedOutTracking()","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that owns and forwards to a Mixpanel SDK"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","title":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}]}}}